  <model metaid="meta_dextromethorphan_intestine" id="dextromethorphan_intestine" name="Dextromethorphan (DXM) intestine model" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Intestine model of the oral absorption of dextromethorphan</h1>
        <p>An oral dose dissolves and passes the stomach with the rate <code>Ka_dis_dxm</code>
into the lumen of the small intestine, from which the fraction <code>F_dxm_abs</code>
is absorbed into the portal plasma with the rate <code>DXMABS_k</code>, the rest is
excreted in the feces. The oral bioavailability is the fraction absorbed
times the fraction which escapes the first pass through the liver; the
first pass of dextromethorphan is hepatic, the intestinal CYP3A4 is a few
tenths of a percent of a dose and is not part of the model.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
